# CampusShield frontend — environment template
#
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. .env is git-ignored; never commit real values.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A note on what belongs here, and what never does
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is Firebase's PUBLIC web configuration. Vite inlines any
# VITE_-prefixed variable into the JavaScript bundle, so all of it is visible to
# anyone who opens developer tools. That is expected and safe: these values
# identify the project, they do not authorise anything. VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY is
# an identifier despite its name — it is not a secret and cannot be used to read
# or write data on its own.
#
# What protects the system is the ID token the browser obtains after a real
# sign-in, verified server-side by the Firebase Admin SDK, and the role read from
# identity.app_user rather than from anything the browser says about itself.
#
# NEVER put in this file, or anywhere under frontend/:
#   - a service-account JSON file or any part of one
#   - FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_PATH / FIREBASE_CREDENTIALS_JSON
#   - a private key, database URL, or any server-side pepper
# Those belong in backend/.env, which is read by a process the browser cannot see.
# A service-account key placed here would be published to every visitor and can
# mint a token for any user in the project.
#
# Values come from: Firebase console → Project settings → General →
# Your apps → Web app → SDK setup and configuration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend API
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must appear in the backend's CORS_ORIGINS list, or the browser blocks every
# request before the server sees it.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/v1
